{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1515-hunter-the-reckoning-story-ideas","id":1515,"title":"Hunter: The Reckoning Story Ideas","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-02T21:33:47-07:00","id":1515,"title":"Hunter: The Reckoning Story Ideas","content":"So, these threads were always my favourite in the past forum, so let's not let them die!<br /> <br /> H:tR is a bit more tricky than some other games, but I'm sure we can think of something.<ul><li>A group of imbued has been fighting the monsters that rule their small town. They finally corner one demon, and by a stroke of luck manage to kill it. As the body lies on the ground, it slowly shifts back to a human: more specifically a human who has been doing work with charity in the area. No other monster they've managed to take down has done this: the bodies either collapse into dust or remain monstrous, at least to the Second Sight.</li> <li>Some Imbued happen across a whole town of Imbued. Investigating closer reveals that the whole town was Awoken at once, and very quickly obliterated all the monsters in their midst, and have been making raids to other towns in the area. For a group used to being few in number and largely isolated, this is a game-changer. Of course, one has to question, why the chage? Suspicions grow deeper when it becomes known that they all received the same message: &quot;STAND AGAINST THE OTHERS&quot;...</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-24T13:31:00-07:00","id":179197,"title":"","content":"A Wayward unknowingly has a brain tumor that convinces her that there are monster everywhere. Which leads to a wave of innocent people being killed (and a guilty one or two). Can the PCs stop her before any more innocents die?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-24T14:52:38-07:00","id":179267,"title":"","content":"-A group of hunters is stablished in an area, one of the hunters is dating a guy. they are still very new and still learning of their powers, one of the hunters gets pregnant from this man and finds out that he is a werewolf. will the group hunt down the father to be? will they get rid of the unborn child? will it become an abomination?<br /> <br /> - A group of hunters has tracked down a Spirit on a haunted X (House/Bar/Car Etc...) and they dont know how to fight it or fail when they face him. They look for information about this manifestation. While doing their research they get a message from Hunter-Net, from a man who claims he can help them to stop this aparition...as long as they help him to get rid of a vampire, this user's name is Carpenter169","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":1754,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","user":"Crowley","date":". 06-24-2014, 06:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-24T15:19:44-07:00","id":179272,"title":"","content":"Shock's thread at the general forum had a really creepy illegal 'blood milking' operation detailed. I think that something like that would be quite true WoD's themes<br /> and a great way to show your players that not all evil is supernatural in origin.<br /> <br /> Besides the inherent creepy factor it would be easy to turn it into Vampire run operation if its what the ST wants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1700-blue-fox","name":"Blue Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1700_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-24T16:57:37-07:00","id":179339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1515-hunter-the-reckoning-story-ideas?p=179267#post179267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- A group of hunters has tracked down a Spirit on a haunted X (House/Bar/Car Etc...) and they dont know how to fight it or fail when they face him. They look for information about this manifestation. While doing their research they get a message from Hunter-Net, from a man who claims he can help them to stop this aparition...as long as they help him to get rid of a vampire, this user's name is Carpenter169</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes to anything with Carpenter in it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-24T20:07:00-07:00","id":179426,"title":"","content":"can someone summon bates up so he can give us his badass seal of aproval? HOW MANY VIRGINS AND JACK DANIELS DO WE NEED TO SUMMON HIM UP?!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T08:58:40-07:00","id":179760,"title":"","content":"-The hunters start to hear rumors of a haunting at a local theatre. Upon investigating these rumors they find out that one of the understudy's has become a star overnight, and is acting strangely. She has been observed talking to a man that no one can see or hear. Is she crazy, or is there something else at work here?<br /> <br /> -A series of arsons in the city have been turning up burned bodies that investigators are having difficulty identifying. Images of the burned buildings show markings in soot that are definitely Hunter symbols. Most common among them is the one for &quot;Bloodsucker&quot; or &quot;Vampire&quot;. These arsons are being perpetrated dangerously close to innocent residences. Could there be a hunter on the loose that is unconcerned with collateral damage when taking out his targets?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I play forum games! Come check out the (mis?)adventures of<br /> Jensven Vargsmed and his canine companion, Shadow in &quot;Forging a Nation&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\"> IC</a>)<br /> ...or the <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/w82hi22ad33hanu/Necro.doc?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Prodigal of Ashen Remorse</a> in &quot;Emerald Labyrinth&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/416995-ic-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","name":"Belkra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1146_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T13:48:41-07:00","id":184052,"title":"","content":"- Your characters have been fairly successful in their endeavors. However, somewhere along the lines they slip up and get caught. After they are drilled for questions, they are deemed insane and sent to a mental ward owned by Pentex. Various Famori Wraith etc. Make residency here. They need to find a way to get out, while eliminating the &quot;bad guys&quot;. Inspired by American horror story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2714-feral-gangrel","name":"Feral Gangrel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T00:39:09-07:00","id":185404,"title":"","content":"-A local &quot;pillar of the community&quot; has gone missing. The PC's suspect supernatural involvement, and the trail leads them to the haven of a Nosferatu. The Nosferatu has been using him as an unwilling blood doll, keeping him in a cell in an abandoned bomb shelter. The Nosferatu attempts to convince the PCs to leave, saying that the man is a pedophile and a rapist, who has so far evaded justice. It should come as little surprise that the Nosferatu was one of the abuser's former victims, though he won't admit this in front of the man (Though the man already suspects.) So far, the Nosferatu has treated the man well, aside from terrifying him with his appearance, and the use of Potence to subdue the man during an escape attempt. He keeps him well fed, and the cell clean, not so unlike a modern prison (Although he hasn't seen the sun since the abduction.) The Nosferatu obviously can't allow the man to leave, since that would breach the Masquerade, and will prevent him from leaving with his powers and a large number of huge ghouled rats. In a few days one of the pedophile's victims will be arrested in connection to the disappearance, who happened to be nearby when the pedophile was kidnapped by the nosferatu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1078,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","user":"Froggy711","date":". 07-01-2014, 03:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}